{# The probe prints a different number on every build - but the cache serves the same body twice, which defeats the crawl's random-word double-draw check: its two draws agree and differ from the stored copy. So the crawl marks this page uncomparable by name instead, in getRegressionGo's list. #} {$stamp}<?php // A body that is different on every build: nanoseconds. Two fetches answering with the // same body therefore prove the second came from the cache, not from a build. $stamp = hrtime ( TRUE );?>